        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "Today in the news, an artist announces his plan to install a monument to Charlie Kirk in Times Square this fall. Let's just say the renderings don't bode well. Meanwhile, the Trump administration cuts the size of two national monuments in Utah â€” rich with rock art and sacred land â€” by a staggering 90% while also pushing for \"energy development\" in the area. Also: A docudrama attempts to shed new light on Caravaggio's life, Required Reading, Art Movements, and lots more. â€”Hakim Bishara, editor-in-chief Artistâ€™s Planned Monument to Charlie Kirk Gets Trolled Online New York City sculptor Sergio Furnari is being raked over the coals online over his plan to unveil a memorial sculpture of slain right-wing podcaster Charlie Kirk in Times Square. Thousands have flocked to Furnariâ€™s Instagram comments to troll and threaten the forthcoming memorial, which will reportedly be unveiled on September 10 in recognition of the first anniversary of Kirkâ€™s assassination. Read More SPONSORED The ICA at VCU Brings Immersive Installation â€œDeo Vindiceâ€ to Richmond The gallery-sized installation at the Institute for Contemporary Art combines Greek mythology with Civil War history to examine white supremacy and hegemonic power. Learn more News The Trump administration has significantly diminished the size of two national monuments in Utah that hold sacred lands and rich archaeological sites. The Manhattan DA said three antiquities are being repatriated to Mexico . One of them was previously held by the Metropolitan Museum of Art. From Our Critics The Artists Working in Velvet, Amethyst, and Relics An exhibition showcases works by Sky Hopinka, vanessa german, April Bey, and others that have connections to spiritual practƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;sTOdhwmldjsgTQY9J5n_wxTeYo4LMN20qGZZTVQQwAkƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AD7bvwgBr